WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.745 --> 00:00:04.680
140 at msu's working hall.

00:00:06.449 --> 00:00:09.552
&gt;&gt; So, he entered the classroom

00:00:09.819 --> 00:00:12.622
from to the back door.

00:00:13.456 --> 00:00:15.625
Where a lot of the students

00:00:15.891 --> 00:00:17.493
that don't sit in the front,

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:18.661
they sit by that backdoor.

00:00:19.462 --> 00:00:22.565
And at that moment, we all kind

00:00:22.832 --> 00:00:22.999
of froze.

00:00:24.467 --> 00:00:26.736
I think somebody said something

00:00:27.003 --> 00:00:29.505
about, you know, a shooter and

00:00:29.772 --> 00:00:32.575
one of my students, and

00:00:32.842 --> 00:00:33.676
everybody panicked.

00:00:34.443 --> 00:00:36.479
Some froze.

00:00:36.746 --> 00:00:39.649
I think a lot of them stood up.

00:00:39.915 --> 00:00:42.618
Some of them froze in place,

00:00:42.885 --> 00:00:44.553
some of them, I don't know if I

00:00:45.054 --> 00:00:47.657
screamed just, you know, find

00:00:47.923 --> 00:00:49.592
cover under the desks.

00:00:50.493 --> 00:00:53.596
A lot of them went under.

00:00:54.597 --> 00:00:57.533
Curled up in a ball under their

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:04.440
chairs and others ran, and the

00:01:04.707 --> 00:01:06.575
guy stepped in about a foot

00:01:06.842 --> 00:01:07.677
inside the classroom.

00:01:07.943 --> 00:01:09.512
Not completely just, like, a

00:01:09.779 --> 00:01:09.879
foot.

00:01:10.579 --> 00:01:11.781
And or even less than a foot.

00:01:12.515 --> 00:01:14.450
Enough that I could see this

00:01:14.717 --> 00:01:19.488
figure, and it was so horrible

00:01:19.755 --> 00:01:21.590
because, you know, when you see

00:01:21.857 --> 00:01:23.693
someone who's totally masked,

00:01:23.959 --> 00:01:25.528
you don't see their face, you

00:01:25.795 --> 00:01:27.463
don't see their hands, you

00:01:27.730 --> 00:01:29.665
don't see, it was like seeing a

00:01:29.932 --> 00:01:30.032
robot.

00:01:30.466 --> 00:01:32.668
It was like seeing something in

00:01:32.935 --> 00:01:34.670
human standing there, and all I

00:01:34.937 --> 00:01:37.740
could see was this silvery kind

00:01:38.007 --> 00:01:41.577
of steel shine weapon.

00:01:42.478 --> 00:01:43.679
I don't think it was a pistol,

00:01:43.946 --> 00:01:45.481
I think it was something larger

00:01:45.748 --> 00:01:45.915
than that.

00:01:46.482 --> 00:01:48.651
And then I could hear the shots,

00:01:48.918 --> 00:01:50.553
and they were just as loud as

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:52.788
the ones in the hallway.

00:01:53.456 --> 00:01:55.825
It was just a nightmare.

00:01:57.526 --> 00:02:00.529
I think everybody under

00:02:00.796 --> 00:02:01.497
adrenaline did whatever they

00:02:01.764 --> 00:02:02.531
could.

00:02:02.798 --> 00:02:05.468
I don't know how long he stood

00:02:05.735 --> 00:02:06.502
there.

00:02:06.769 --> 00:02:07.770
Probably, I mean, he shot at

00:02:08.537 --> 00:02:09.505
least 15 shots.

00:02:10.506 --> 00:02:11.640
One after the other, one after

00:02:11.907 --> 00:02:12.908
the other, one after the other.

00:02:14.510 --> 00:02:15.611
Bang, bang, bang.

00:02:15.878 --> 00:02:17.446
He stepped out and at that

00:02:17.713 --> 00:02:18.714
moment, because I don't recall

00:02:18.981 --> 00:02:20.683
what I did between him starting

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:21.851
to shoot and what I'm going to

00:02:22.118 --> 00:02:22.718
tell you just now.

00:02:23.452 --> 00:02:25.621
I just, my intuition told me

00:02:25.888 --> 00:02:26.756
he's walking down the hall and

00:02:27.022 --> 00:02:28.557
he's going to enter through the

00:02:28.824 --> 00:02:28.924
door.

00:02:29.191 --> 00:02:30.659
I'm closest to it, so I threw

00:02:30.926 --> 00:02:33.496
myself at that door and I

00:02:33.763 --> 00:02:35.564
squatted, and I held the door

00:02:35.831 --> 00:02:37.633
like this, so that my weight

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:39.735
would keep it from and I was

00:02:40.002 --> 00:02:41.637
putting my foot on the wall,

00:02:41.904 --> 00:02:43.572
and holding like this, so that

00:02:43.839 --> 00:02:44.774
he couldn't open it.

00:02:45.441 --> 00:02:47.676
All the time, aware that he

00:02:47.943 --> 00:02:50.546
could just shoot the door

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:51.514
handle and open it.

00:02:51.781 --> 00:02:52.681
But the only thing I thought I

00:02:52.948 --> 00:02:53.549
could do was that.

00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:56.552
At least attempt to stop it.

00:02:57.453 --> 00:03:00.556
And that lasted for about ten

00:03:00.823 --> 00:03:03.492
minutes, felt like an eternity.

00:03:03.759 --> 00:03:04.727
Or 12 minutes.

00:03:04.994 --> 00:03:07.596
In the meantime, I told my

00:03:07.863 --> 00:03:10.666
students and that, I remember.

00:03:10.933 --> 00:03:11.734
I told the students, just

00:03:12.001 --> 00:03:12.701
escape through the windows.

00:03:12.968 --> 00:03:13.836
Kick the windows open, escape

00:03:14.103 --> 00:03:14.670
through the windows.

00:03:15.538 --> 00:03:21.710
And the first line of windows

00:03:21.977 --> 00:03:25.481
closer to the row of seats

00:03:25.748 --> 00:03:26.682
could not be kicked.

00:03:26.949 --> 00:03:27.783
I mean, cannot be broken.

00:03:28.584 --> 00:03:29.552
They're made out a very hard

00:03:29.819 --> 00:03:29.919
glass.

00:03:30.586 --> 00:03:32.588
Probably for, you know,

00:03:32.788 --> 00:03:32.988
insulation.

00:03:33.455 --> 00:03:35.624
So, they attempted and they

00:03:35.891 --> 00:03:37.560
couldn't open those, but then

00:03:37.827 --> 00:03:39.628
the second set of windows

00:03:39.895 --> 00:03:41.630
higher up, they were open and

00:03:41.897 --> 00:03:43.599
there was an opening big enough,

00:03:43.866 --> 00:03:44.800
so they started escaping that

00:03:45.067 --> 00:03:45.134
way.

00:03:45.501 --> 00:03:47.469
In the meantime, the rest,

00:03:47.736 --> 00:03:48.871
there were quite a few on the

00:03:49.138 --> 00:03:51.540
floor wounded, and I had some

00:03:51.807 --> 00:03:54.643
kids that were very heroic.

00:03:55.477 --> 00:03:56.612
That were helping those that

00:03:56.879 --> 00:03:58.614
were wounded and some of them,

00:03:58.881 --> 00:04:00.649
I don't know much about how to,

00:04:00.916 --> 00:04:02.751
you know, what paramedics do or

00:04:03.018 --> 00:04:04.620
what you do in a situation like

00:04:04.854 --> 00:04:06.622
that, but my students kind of

00:04:06.755 --> 00:04:07.723
knew what to do, so they were

00:04:07.990 --> 00:04:09.491
trying to cover their wounds

00:04:09.758 --> 00:04:10.626
with their hands, so they

00:04:10.759 --> 00:04:11.160
wouldn't bleed to death.

00:04:12.628 --> 00:04:14.630
I think I will be haunted by

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:14.797
it.

00:04:15.464 --> 00:04:17.533
I definitely don't want to go

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:19.501
to --

00:04:19.768 --> 00:04:21.537
because I couldn't go into that

00:04:21.804 --> 00:04:22.638
classroom after what I saw.

00:04:23.472 --> 00:04:25.507
I think the administration is

00:04:25.774 --> 00:04:26.642
going to move my class to a

00:04:26.909 --> 00:04:27.643
different building.

00:04:28.644 --> 00:04:29.545
At the same time, but a

00:04:29.812 --> 00:04:30.145
different building.

00:04:30.646 --> 00:04:33.515
I don't know if I will be

00:04:33.782 --> 00:04:35.484
nervous every time I teach.

00:04:36.652 --> 00:04:38.654
I don't know if I will, I don't

00:04:38.888 --> 00:04:39.855
know what the university is

00:04:40.122 --> 00:04:40.656
going to do.

00:04:40.856 --> 00:04:42.658
They are going to put locks in

00:04:42.725 --> 00:04:43.692
rooms, so that you can lock the

00:04:43.959 --> 00:04:44.660
room from the inside.

00:04:45.461 --> 00:04:46.762
I think that's one of the

00:04:47.029 --> 00:04:47.763
things that might happen.

00:04:48.664 --> 00:04:50.666
I don't know that means we are

